course: dictionary
lesson: 7012
title: Parental, meaning of or from parents
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Parental is an adjective, so it tells you more about a noun. It means of or about parents, or coming from a parent. Look at «Most consoles have parental controls that can block games above a chosen age rating.» The controls belong to parents, so parental controls are settings that parents can use.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «Parental consent» means permission from a parent, and «parental leave» means time off work for a parent. Ask yourself: what does the word after it belong to? Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Parental also appears in science. Parental care is the way animal or human parents look after their young. A bird that feeds its chicks is showing parental care. The same idea can help you work out other words that start with parent.
fact: Parental means of or about parents, or from a parent.
fact: «Parental controls» are settings on devices that limit what children can see or play.
fact: «Parental consent» means permission from a parent.
fact: Parental care is the way animal or human parents look after their young.
fact: «Parental guidance (PG)» is a film rating in the UK, and it tells families that parents may want to think about what children watch.
exercise: «Most consoles have parental controls that can block games above a chosen age rating.» In parental controls, what does parental mean? | Made of wood | *Of or from parents | Very quick | Sad
exercise: Ella reads about parental care in animals. What does it mean? | *The way animal parents look after their young | Animals that live in water | Animals who are very old | A kind of food for pets
exercise: «Parental leave» is time off work for a parent. Which word means of or from parents? | off | *parental | leave | time
test: «Parental consent» means permission from whom? | A teacher | A shopkeeper | *A parent | A doctor
test: Which is a parental control? | A rule about feeding the fish | *A setting on a device that limits what children can see | A game that is always free | A bag for carrying books to school
exam: In «parental guidance (PG)», what does parental mean? | Lost or hidden away | Loud and noisy | *Of or about parents, so parents may want to guide what children watch | Very new and shiny
